        "id": 127630,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-15T04:54:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Greywind\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/greywind/48/2006_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Greywind:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Foote wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Silverleaf. How are we going to PT and test and print 2-3 more expansions in a year with the final one already confirmed to be mega? I just don't see it as feasible</blockquote></div>\nWe have three things confirmed for this year for playtest. We have an approximation of two years until the end of SotM's projected run. Easily feasible. \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Spirit Island. Villains of the Multiverse. Broken City plus For Profit. The Tactics add-on that I can't remember the name of. I count 4, or possibly 5, and that's without knowing what else is in the pipeline.</p>",
