      {
        "id": 127633,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-15T14:24:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is the final one being mega confirmed?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes it has been confirmed. Somewhere. It must have been in an interview or something because I'm having trouble finding a link to provide you. I know its been said before.</p>\n<p>Also I have some relevant info from when Vengeance was announced on the ST Kickstarter:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<span>To give you some insights into what we're doing here at Greater Than Games, going forward, it is our intent to release expansions for Sentinels of the Multiverse roughly once per year until we reach the end of the story arc for the game. This schedule, which is slightly slower than what we've done in the past, will free up resources to print other games unrelated to Sentinels of the Multiverse. (But still super awesome; just you wait!) \n</span></blockquote>\n&nbsp;",
